QUE:-2 Describe CSS selectors and list the types of selectores?

   ANS    -> CSS selectors are patterns used to select the HTML elements that you want to style. The 

selector targets the elements in the HTML document, and then the styles defined in the CSS rule 

are applied to those elements. CSS selectors allow you to apply styles based on various 

factors, such as element type, class, ID, attribute, or relationships between elements

                Type of selectors:-

  1 Universal Selector (*)                9 Group Selector (,)

  2 Class Selector (.)                 

  3 ID Selector (#)

  4 Child Selector (>)

  5 General Sibling Selector (~)

  6 Attribute Selector ([])

  7 Pseudo-class Selector (:)

  8 Pseudo-element Selector (::)

